So the total read is `ceil(chunk.height / y_sampling) * floor(chunk.width / x_sampling) * bpc`.

But the allocation is `floor(chunk.height / y_sampling) * floor(chunk.width / x_sampling) * bpc` (approximately, since `chansz = bpc * width * height / (x_sampling * y_sampling)` uses integer division).

